      "traceTextDiagram": "Skills Framework Execution\n├── Main() generic entry point \u003c-- 4a\n│   └── mainWithCode() core execution \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/skillmain/main.go:98\n│       ├── buildRunContext() setup \u003c-- 4b\n│       │   ├── Load CAS store \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/skillmain/main.go:209\n│       │   ├── Create path validator \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/skillmain/main.go:233\n│       │   └── Initialize validator \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/skillmain/main.go:248\n│       ├── JSON input parsing \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/skillmain/main.go:141\n│       ├── Struct validation \u003c-- 4c\n│       └── run() skill execution \u003c-- 4d\n│           └── skillout.Emit() output \u003c-- skills/git_status/main.go:86\n│               └── envelope.OK() creation \u003c-- 4e\n└── Error handling path \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/skillmain/main.go:167\n    └── envelope.Error() on failure \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/skillout/emit.go:29",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nThe skills framework solves the **execution consistency problem** for agent tools. When agents need to run git operations, file diffs, or other skills, they need a standardized way to handle input validation, path security, error formatting, and large output storage. Without this framework, each skill would reinvent these concerns, leading to inconsistent behavior and potential security issues.\n\n## Details\n\nThe framework uses a **generic entry point** [4a] that handles all skills through a common pipeline. First, it builds a **secure execution context** [4b] containing a CAS store for large outputs, a path validator to prevent file system escapes, and a struct validator for input validation. The system then **parses JSON input** from stdin and validates it against struct tags [4c] before executing the actual skill logic [4d].\n\nA key innovation is the **envelope-based output system** [4e] that wraps all results in a standardized JSON format with metadata. When skills produce large outputs like git diffs, the framework automatically detects size limits and stores the content in **content-addressable storage** while returning a digest for retrieval. This keeps agent responses fast while preserving full data access.\n\nThe error handling path ensures **graceful failures** with structured error envelopes that include error codes, messages, and helpful hints for debugging."
    }
  ],
